    {
      "title": "Find every sign boundary",
      "body": "<p>Keep the two factors separate. The first vanishes when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>; the second when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>. Work on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "A product changes sign only at a zero of a factor, so all factor zeros belong in the sign chart.",
      "pitfall": "The doubled angle ranges from 0 to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Find and order the three interior boundary points.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l16",
          "reminder": "A product changes sign only at a zero of a factor, so all factor zeros belong in the sign chart."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Build the product sign chart",
      "body": "Test the sign of each factor on the intervals between the zeros you found. Keep an interval when the two signs satisfy the given product inequality.",
      "recap": "A product is nonnegative when its factors have the same sign, or one is zero.",
      "pitfall": "The number of accepted pieces is not the fraction of the domain; compare their lengths.",
      "pause": "Find all accepted intervals, add their lengths and divide by the full interval length.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l04",
          "reminder": "A product is nonnegative when its factors have the same sign, or one is zero."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>The first factor has zeros <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math> and is positive between them. The second has zero <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> and is negative before it, positive after it.</p><p>The product is nonnegative on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0222A;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>. The total accepted length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>Dividing by the full length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>: <strong>C.</strong></p>",
